          "filename": "Refuelling Donaghadee lifeboat - geograph.org.uk - 815924.jpg",
          "caption": "Refuelling Donaghadee lifeboat. Lifeboats are expected always to have a full tank of fuel.  At stations with an all-weather boat, where there is no convenient supply (for example in a marina) or no suitable place for a tank, refuelling is by means of a bowser hauled by a tractor or Land Rover.  The antennae of the lifeboat 815880 can be seen behind the crew member.  Any spilled fuel is cleaned up afterwards to avoid pollution.",
